block content
    h1 Hiatal Hernia
    p Definition by #[a(href="https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/hiatal-hernia/symptoms-causes/syc-20373379") Mayo Clinic]:
    blockquote A hiatal hernia occurs when the upper part of your stomach bulges through the large muscle separating your abdomen and chest (diaphragm). Your diaphragm has a small opening (hiatus) through which your food tube (esophagus) passes before connecting to your stomach. In a hiatal hernia, the stomach pushes up through that opening and into your chest.

